cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Aerolume in research, please cite the software as below and
  name the version you used. The methods and their references are in
  docs/methods.md; the validation evidence is in docs/validation.md. Every
  result Aerolume saves records its own provenance (version, settings hash,
  device, precision), which a paper's methods section can quote.
type: software
title: "Aerolume: an open-source aerodynamics studio with GPU Navier-Stokes solvers, airfoil polars and finite-wing analysis"
abstract: >-
  Aerolume is a desktop studio and Python library for 2D and 3D
  aerodynamics. It solves the incompressible Navier-Stokes equations on
  uniform staggered grids in PyTorch (GPU or CPU) with immersed bodies by
  Brinkman penalisation, an exact pressure projection and SSP-RK3 time
  stepping, plus a Boussinesq energy equation, actuator-disc fans, jets
  and smoke emitters. It computes viscous airfoil polars with an
  XFOIL-class integral boundary-layer method and finite wings with a
  vortex lattice and a nonlinear lifting line. Time averages carry
  batch-means standard errors and grid studies a Roache grid-convergence
  index. Every solver is validated against published benchmarks by one
  script (validation/run_all.py).
authors:
  - name: "Aerolume contributors"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-01"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/TanmayPasula/Aerolume"
url: "https://tanmaypasula.github.io/Aerolume-Website/"
keywords:
  - computational fluid dynamics
  - aerodynamics
  - Navier-Stokes
  - immersed boundary method
  - natural convection
  - actuator disc
  - airfoil polar
  - vortex lattice method
  - grid convergence index
  - PyTorch
